From 6e93a681aad2f5cb526374e57fd4b9628f6e5bd4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Steven Huang <shuang@myai001.mylab.io>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 19:18:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 03/10] perf(sm75): fuse the small-batch hc_pre cast and rms
 statistic into one kernel

hc_pre on decode batches is a compiled chain -- to_copy (fp32 cast),
two reductions and a pointwise, about 4 launches per layer per step
over [<=16, hc*hc*hidden] fp32, ~70 us of launch-latency-bound device
time per stage per step. _hc_prenorm_smallm_kernel folds the cast and
the sum-of-squares into one pass; the mix linear stays torch, so the
mix values round exactly as before and only the summation order of
mean(x^2) changes (fp32, ~6e-8 on rsqrt, x_flat bit-identical).

Gated on B <= 16 -- above that inductor's tiled reductions win -- and
on the flat bf16/fp32 row form the model actually feeds it.
SGLANG_SM75_FUSE_HC_PRE=0 is the A/B switch. Confirmed in the decode
trace of the TP0/PP3 rank: the triton_red_fused chain is gone and
_hc_prenorm_smallm_kernel runs 7.33 times per step.
