The checkpoint ships head.weight bf16, so at vocab 129280 and TP2 every
decode step on the last PP stage streams 530 MB of weight to produce
one row. The measured 0.908 ms is a cuBLAS gemv already at the card's
read ceiling, so fewer bytes is the only lever left. The head is
quantized per 128x128 block at load -- the same recipe every dense
layer uses, done on CPU so the GPU never allocates the fp32 scratch --
and the bf16 copy is freed. The GEMV measures 0.666 ms for the shard
shape against 0.908 ms for the bf16 gemv.

get_embed_and_head raises with the switch named when the head is fp8
(embedding sharing needs the bf16 weight), and set_embed_and_head
re-quantizes after a weight swap. SGLANG_SM75_LMHEAD_FP8=0 keeps the
bf16 head. GSM8K 200-question gate with the whole SM75 stack on:
190/200 (95.0%), invalid 0.5%.
